    "id": "29cbc687573025f128a156cf",
    "path": "tracing_subscriber::registry::Scope::from_root",
    "name": "from_root",
    "owner": "tracing_subscriber::registry::Scope",
    "crate": "tracing-subscriber",
    "version": "0.3.23",
    "kind": "function",
    "signature": "fn from_root(self) -> ScopeFromRoot<'a, R>",
    "docs": "Flips the order of the iterator, so that it is ordered from root to leaf.\n\nThe iterator will first return the root span, then that span's immediate child,\nand so on until it finally returns the span that [`SpanRef::scope`] was called on.\n\nIf any items were consumed from the [`Scope`] before calling this method then they\nwill *not* be returned from the [`ScopeFromRoot`].\n\n**Note**: this will allocate if there are many spans remaining, or if the\n\"smallvec\" feature flag is not enabled.",
